{
  "note": [
    "The §3.1 masking table as data: which fields the vault renders masked, and",
    "therefore which ones fill_secret marks in the page.",
    "",
    "Every case is one raw Bitwarden item and the descriptors the broker must",
    "derive from it. It is asserted against the REAL classifier in",
    "vendor/browser-server/seed_vault_broker/cli.py, through",
    "e2e/fixtures/classifyProbe.py — the only classifier there is. The JS fake",
    "used to carry a second copy of these rules and was asserted alongside; it",
    "now returns whatever a fixture states, so there is nothing left to compare",
    "and nothing left to diverge.",
    "",
    "Shapes and concealment come from the pinned Bitwarden client source, tag",
    "cli-v2026.7.0 (commit 82186c3d92c0da14aa86c848b781d949a8a6202a): item types",
    "in vault/enums/cipher-type.ts, identity keys in models/export/identity.export.ts,",
    "ssh key keys in models/export/ssh-key.export.ts, linked ids in",
    "vault/enums/linked-id-type.enum.ts, and what the client conceals in the",
    "cipher-view templates.",
    "",
    "(commit 2629bcbe1380c894e3a7f52cafcac3988edb8fbb) matches only types 1-5 in",
    "",
    "Consumed by packages/device-core/test/maskClassification.test.ts."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "login",
      "why": "password hidden; username is not; the generated TOTP code is masked even though the client shows it, because an agent fills it and never reads it back; notes are not",
      "bitwarden": {
        "id": "L1",
        "name": "Pizza Login",
        "type": 1,
        "login": {
          "username": "jon",
          "password": "hunter2",
          "totp": "otpauth://totp/x",
          "uris": [
            {
              "uri": "https://pizza.example/"
            }
          ]
        },
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "recovery",
            "type": 1,
            "value": "recovery-code-9f2a"
          },
          {
            "name": "account nickname",
            "type": 0,
            "value": "the pizza one"
          }
        ],
        "notes": "delivery goes to the side door"
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "label": "username",
          "hidden": false,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "email",
          "hidden": false,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": true
        },
        {
          "label": "login",
          "hidden": false,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": true
        },
        {
          "label": "user",
          "hidden": false,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": true
        },
        {
          "label": "password",
          "hidden": true,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "totp",
          "hidden": true,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "recovery",
          "hidden": true,
          "custom": true,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "account nickname",
          "hidden": false,
          "custom": true,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "notes",
          "hidden": false,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "card with a colliding custom field",
      "why": "number and code hidden, and code's aliases with it; expiry, cardholder name and brand not; both a plain custom field and a LINKED one sharing a built-in's name keep their own descriptor AND their own token (custom:cardholder name, custom:number), so either can actually be asked for — a linked field collides exactly as any other custom field does; expiry is this app's composed month from expMonth and expYear, offered only when both parts are well-formed",
      "bitwarden": {
        "id": "C1",
        "name": "Visa",
        "type": 3,
        "card": {
          "number": "4111111111111111",
          "code": "737",
          "expMonth": "04",
          "expYear": "2031",
          "cardholderName": "Jon Doe",
          "brand": "Visa"
        },
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "cardholder name",
            "type": 0,
            "value": "shipping only"
          },
          {
            "name": "number",
            "type": 3,
            "value": null,
            "linkedId": 305
          }
        ]
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "label": "number",
          "hidden": true,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "code",
          "hidden": true,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": false
        },
        {
          "label": "cvv",
          "hidden": true,
          "custom": false,
          "alias": true
        },
        {
          "label": "security code",
          "hidden": true,
